# .gitignore — minimal curated list for this repository
# Purpose: keep the repo small and avoid accidental commits of generated build outputs
# and IDE temp files while allowing CI to produce and upload artifacts.
#
# What is ignored and why:
#  - **/build/** and **/build/libs/**: compiled classes, jars, distributions and other
#    build outputs; these are generated artifacts and should not be committed.
#  - **/build/reports/problems/**: IDE/Gradle problem reports (HTML) are generated and
#    frequently noisy; keep them out of version control.
#  - **/assets.txt**: generated asset index list (created by Gradle task).
#  - **/resource-config.json**: generated by native-image tooling; not a source file.
#  - IDE, OS, and editor temp files (.idea/, *.iml, .DS_Store, etc.) — local-only files.


# Gradle
.gradle/
gradle-app.setting

# Ignore all build output directories (module build folders, jars, reports, etc.)
**/build/

# Explicitly ignore build libs and problem reports (redundant with **/build/, but explicit)
**/build/libs/
**/build/reports/problems/
StumbleHome/lib/build/libs/
StumbleHome/build/reports/problems/

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws

# OS-specific
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Java
*.class
hs_err_pid*
*.log

# Misc editors
*~
*.*#
*#*#

# keep generated asset list out of the repo
**/assets.txt

# Graal native-image resource config (generated)
**/resource-config.json
